{"review_id": "iclr_Jyrwd2wja9_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_Jyrwd2wja9", "passages": [{"quote": "The authors study a relevant problem and connect it nicely to the matrix sensing literature.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem relevance and motivation"}, {"quote": "The article is written in a way which is easy to follow.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity of writing"}, {"quote": "their result on the RIP of perturbed Gaussian matrices can be highlighted. The appeal of the result is that no assumption what soever is put on the pertubation", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "generality of theoretical result"}, {"quote": "I am unaware of a concrete bound like this in the literature.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty of contribution"}, {"quote": "The idea to replace a matrix with its left singular vectors is a very natural one, and it has indeed been proposed before in the literature", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty of method"}, {"quote": "This severely impacts the value of the empirical success of their method.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "significance of empirical results"}, {"quote": "I am not convinced by Lemma 1", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "soundness of theoretical claim"}, {"quote": "Theorems 4 and 5 do little to explain the empirical success of the preconditioning strategy.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "explanatory power of theory"}, {"quote": "the presence of the term √n^2/m in their bound is very limiting. Does this not necessitate the number of measurement to be proportional to n^2", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "scalability of theoretical bound"}, {"quote": "this means that the noise *necessarily* is amplified. A discussion on this, and possible mitigations, such as in (Chen, Lin; 2021) would make the work more complete.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of discussion"}, {"quote": "While the paper generally is well written, it would benefit from another round of proofreading.", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "writing quality"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_WVzYMa68Of_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_WVzYMa68Of", "passages": [{"quote": "Gradient-free adversarial attack is interesting.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem interest"}, {"quote": "The experiment scope is too narrow.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental coverage"}, {"quote": "Motivation is not clear.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of motivation"}, {"quote": "Time complexity is missing.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of analysis"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_WVzYMa68Of_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_WVzYMa68Of", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper introduces a unique combination of Tensor Train (TT) decomposition and PROTES optimization to handle high-dimensional perturbations efficiently in black-box settings.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty of method combination"}, {"quote": "According to the experimental results, the proposed method performs better than some query-based methods.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical performance"}, {"quote": "a fairer and more comprehensive evaluation would involve comparing TETRADAT with transfer-based attack methods.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of baselines"}, {"quote": "it does not provide a detailed comparison of the actual number of queries required to achieve a successful attack across different methods.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "thoroughness of efficiency analysis"}, {"quote": "The complexity of tuning these parameters makes the method less practical for deployment", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "practicality of method"}, {"quote": "This discretization could restrict the method's flexibility", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "design limitation"}, {"quote": "The evaluation is limited to ImageNet, lacking tests on additional datasets", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "generalizability of evaluation"}, {"quote": "The presentation of this paper doesn't meet the ICLR standards and needs further improvement.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "presentation quality"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_WVzYMa68Of_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_WVzYMa68Of", "passages": [{"quote": "This method outperforms three baseline methods (Onepixel, Square, and Pixle) in attack tasks across seven models, including adversarially trained models.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical performance"}, {"quote": "This method focuses only on the key pixels, keeping the adversarial attacks not being observed by human eyes, which allows it to achieve high success rate with minimal image distortion.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "perceptual quality"}, {"quote": "the study focuses on untargeted attacks. It also needs to consider and compare with the targeted attack results.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "scope of evaluation"}, {"quote": "the paper does not address if the approach is feasible for larger and deeper models.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "scalability analysis"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_WVzYMa68Of_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_WVzYMa68Of", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper is easy to understand.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity of writing"}, {"quote": "The paper is logically expressed, and the description of the method is complete and intuitive.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "presentation quality"}, {"quote": "the method proposed in this paper is not innovative enough.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty of contribution"}, {"quote": "it relies primarily on the PROTES optimiser, as described in the paper by Batsheva et al.[1], without making any innovative modifications to the PROTES algorithm itself.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "originality of technical approach"}, {"quote": "the concept of using saliency maps for such attacks is not new.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty of approach"}, {"quote": "The paper utilizes Onepixel, Pixle, and Square as baselines for comparison, all of which focus on perturbing a small number of pixels to achieve adversarial attacks. However, the paper lacks a comparison with query-based black-box attack methods", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of baselines"}, {"quote": "there is a noticeable absence of ablation studies that demonstrate the effectiveness of incorporating the attribution maps.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "thoroughness of ablation study"}, {"quote": "there is a lack of textual analysis to accompany these results.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "depth of result discussion"}, {"quote": "The average L1 and L2 norms reported for the TETRADAT method in Tables 2 and 3 do not appear to demonstrate a clear advantage over the baseline methods.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "strength of empirical results"}, {"quote": "this claim lacks evidence, as the authors have not provided any experiments with human observers to back up the assertion", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "support for claims"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_c8sEgxG2c0_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_c8sEgxG2c0", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper is well-written and well-structured, making it easy to read and understand.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity and structure"}, {"quote": "The figures are of high quality, and the overall presentation is excellent.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "presentation quality"}, {"quote": "I would highly recommend these sections to newcomers in the field as they provide an excellent and comprehensive tutorial", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "pedagogical value"}, {"quote": "The ablation study is also well-executed and thoroughly detailed.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "thoroughness of ablation study"}, {"quote": "The technical decisions seem sound, and I trust the overall technical quality of the work.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "soundness of technical approach"}, {"quote": "The paper lacks significant research contributions.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty of contribution"}, {"quote": "they primarily utilize existing codebases. Consequently, this represents good engineering practice rather than a novel research contribution.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "originality of implementation"}, {"quote": "similar ablations have been performed extensively in the literature", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty of ablation study"}, {"quote": "the dataset is not adequately discussed, with minimal information provided.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "description of dataset"}, {"quote": "The experimental protocol focuses on three specific tasks, while the model is intended to be generic.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "breadth of evaluation"}, {"quote": "The authors do not discuss the pre-training data or the extent of overlap between the downstream datasets and the pre-training datasets for each model", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "transparency of experimental setup"}, {"quote": "the publication lacks sufficient contributions for a conference like ICLR.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "significance for venue"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_c8sEgxG2c0_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_c8sEgxG2c0", "passages": [{"quote": "the observation of the relative performance of causal language model performance being better than masked language is very interesting", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "interest of finding"}, {"quote": "I think the species identification task in Table 1 is an interesting approach.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty of evaluation task"}, {"quote": "I think the codon usage experiment in Figure 8 is interesting. I do think it conveys that their model better adheres to context.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "insightfulness of experiment"}, {"quote": "Figure 1 on it's own is not a great selling point to me, as it does not tell me the quality of the results.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "informativeness of figure"}, {"quote": "The test described in Figure 2b is incongruent with the rest of the paper.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "coherence of experimental design"}, {"quote": "It's difficult to see how this discriminative test translates to the modern generative modeling case.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "relevance of experiment"}, {"quote": "Since the speed of GenomeOcean is strongly advertised, it'd be great to have an ablation study of the improvements that made the model what % faster.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of ablation study"}, {"quote": "I think the ORF length analysis is quite weak.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "strength of analysis"}]}
{"review_id": "ANCH-1", "paper_id": "ANCH-1", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper tackles an interesting problem.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem interest"}, {"quote": "the experimental evaluation is thorough, covering five datasets with proper ablations.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "thoroughness of evaluation"}, {"quote": "the novelty is limited: the proposed method is a straightforward combination of two existing techniques.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty of method"}, {"quote": "The writing is also difficult to follow in Sections 3-4, with undefined notation.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of writing"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_c8sEgxG2c0_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_c8sEgxG2c0", "passages": [{"quote": "GenomeOcean appears to have a large advantage over other generative models in creating sequences", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical performance"}, {"quote": "GenomeOcean can generate genome sequences quickly, and is 80x faster than existing models of similar size.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "inference efficiency"}, {"quote": "Poorly motivated in terms of use cases", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of motivation"}, {"quote": "Using GUE to determine which tokenization, model architecture, and training objective to be used for the generative model seems arbitrary and potentially incongruous.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "validity of design choices"}, {"quote": "The representations learned using these modeling decisions will be optimized for the relatively narrow set of tasks presented in GUE, and may have very little generalizability.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "generalizability of approach"}, {"quote": "the authors should also consider CNN-based architectures such as GPN (Benegas et. al, 2023) or LOGO (Yang et. al, 2022).", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of baselines"}, {"quote": "The results from the biological properties investigation are not significant", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "strength of results"}, {"quote": "there needs to be a more comprehensive effort to evaluate the "goodness" of the generated genomes in this paper. Currently, there is too much emphasis on model design and not enough emphasis on validation.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "balance of evaluation"}, {"quote": "The main context benchmarks in 4.1 are inherently better suited to the biases of GenomeOcean", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "fairness of comparison"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_c8sEgxG2c0_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_c8sEgxG2c0", "passages": [{"quote": "The authors benchmark several architectural decisions that are commonly made in genomic foundation modelling. Despite the concerns highlighted below, this type of benchmark is likely of high significance to the community", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "significance of benchmark"}, {"quote": "The authors successfully combine several recent efficiency improvements to vastly improve sequence generation speed.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "technical achievement"}, {"quote": "Proposed metrics for evaluating quality of generated sequences are to my knowledge novel and a good initial attempt at addressing a difficult yet relevant problem.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty of evaluation metrics"}, {"quote": "GenomeOcean shows outperformance in the selected metrics compared to existing generative genomic foundation models.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical performance"}, {"quote": "The addition of the Reorder baseline alleviates concerns about shortcut learning on chemical characteristics", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "rigor of experimental design"}, {"quote": "The paper omits any statistical or textual description of the pre-training dataset, other than the method of collection, making it difficult to form intuition about the biological validity of experiments", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "description of dataset"}, {"quote": "the choice to evaluate performance on the Genome Understanding Evaluation benchmark may dilute the insights gained.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "appropriateness of benchmark"}, {"quote": "Without this step, data leakage may occur, and it becomes unclear whether the models are truly capturing biological function / structure.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "validity of evaluation"}, {"quote": "using other genomic foundation models as a method to discriminate generated sequences may be a limitation, as the metric would suffer from inherent biases in the existing FMs.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "limitation of evaluation metric"}, {"quote": "the tasks evaluated (e.g. species classification) lack strong correlation with the functional validity of the generated sequences", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "relevance of evaluation tasks"}, {"quote": "claims in the introduction that genomic foundation models outperform classic supervised models are unsubstantiated. For splice site prediction specifically, **none of the in-line citations provided mention splice site detection.**", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "accuracy of claims"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_1cM0yQe3pO_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_1cM0yQe3pO", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper is well-structured and easy to read.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity and structure"}, {"quote": "The proposed method integrates VAE and flow matching in a straightforward manner, offering novelty in its ability to learn vector fields with uncertainty.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty of approach"}, {"quote": "the high performance on MNIST and CIFAR-10 datasets suggests that the hypotheses and approaches of this study are reasonably valid.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical validation"}, {"quote": "it is necessary to clarify the setting that assumes such overlapping vector fields.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of assumptions"}, {"quote": "The uncertainty involving deterministic flows crossing and the possibility of tracing different flows from the initial value (i.e., the x0 and x1 pairings are not unique) appear to be mixed.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of problem formulation"}, {"quote": "during inference, z is sampled from the prior and thus is not determined solely by x0. As a result, the model could reach a different x1, which may not be desirable", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "soundness of inference"}, {"quote": "This implies a significantly larger number of learnable parameters compared to existing models", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "parameter efficiency"}, {"quote": "it is not entirely fair in terms of parameter count relative to previous research", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "fairness of comparison"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_1cM0yQe3pO_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_1cM0yQe3pO", "passages": [{"quote": "Clear, easy-to-follow presentation with strong empirical performance compared to baseline methods.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity and empirical results"}, {"quote": "The motivation of the paper is unclear, particularly in the Introduction.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of motivation"}, {"quote": "The statement at line 73, "Importantly, variational rectified flow matching differs in that it enables modeling ambiguity in the data-space-time-space domain, i.e., the goal is a model where flow trajectories can intersect," does not clarify how allowing flow trajectories to intersect resolves the ambiguity problem.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of key claim"}, {"quote": "VAEs are known to sometimes experience mode collapse, where the same high-density velocities may be generated from multiple modes of z. How does the proposed method handle this issue?", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "handling of known limitation"}, {"quote": "I suggest including a "diversity metric" in the experimental protocol to measure the variety of generated samples.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of evaluation"}, {"quote": "Are there any theoretical or methodological benefits of the proposed approach compared to these methods? Without such justification, it's difficult to attribute the improved performance to the additional variable z.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "justification of approach"}, {"quote": "There is no theoretical guarantee that the proposed approach will achieve a better straight flow when addressing the ambiguity problem.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "lack of theoretical guarantee"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_1cM0yQe3pO_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_1cM0yQe3pO", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper presents a valuable observation: because the vector field is parameterized via a Gaussian at each data-domain-time-domain location, ambiguity cannot be captured.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "insight of observation"}, {"quote": "The analytical experiments with visualizations are well-executed and contribute significantly to validating the theoretical analysis.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "quality of experiments"}, {"quote": "Current evaluations are too weak and this paper lacks enough experiments on more real-world and complex datasets, such as the AFHQ, CelebA and ImageNet datasets.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "scope of evaluation"}, {"quote": "The authors should sufficiently discuss these missing related works [1][2][3][4][5], and compare with them in the experiments.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "coverage of related work"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_1cM0yQe3pO_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_1cM0yQe3pO", "passages": [{"quote": "This paper addresses a notable limitation in flow matching models, specifically the ambiguity at path intersections that results in curved sampling trajectories.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "significance of problem"}, {"quote": "By tackling this ambiguity, the proposed approach demonstrates clear improvements over existing rectified flow models, particularly in low NFE settings.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "strength of improvements"}, {"quote": "The paper is well-written and easy to follow, clearly presenting concepts.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity of writing"}, {"quote": "Interpreting the flow-matching objective through variational inference to reduce directional ambiguity is conceptually sound", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "soundness of approach"}, {"quote": "In line 53, the authors claim, "This results in trajectories that are more straight". It is unclear why reducing ambiguity would inherently lead to straighter flows.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "justification of claim"}, {"quote": "the paper should include proofs demonstrating that the learned distribution from VRFM preserves the marginal data distribution", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of theory"}, {"quote": "The empirical evaluation is restricted to MNIST and CIFAR-10, which limits the generalizability of the findings.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "generalizability of evaluation"}, {"quote": "the reported results of VRFM in low NFE regimes (e.g., 104 FID for 2 NFE on CIFAR-10) are less compelling, given the recent advances [1,2,3] in reducing sampling costs", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "competitiveness of results"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_KmphHE92wU_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_KmphHE92wU", "passages": [{"quote": "The writing is well-organized and generally reader-friendly.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity of writing"}, {"quote": "The theoretical analysis is comprehensive and detailed.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "thoroughness of theory"}, {"quote": "The datasets used in the experiments are somewhat limited.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "scope of evaluation"}, {"quote": "The proposed method would be more convincing if validated on a wider range of datasets, such as PATTERN, CLUSTER, or MolHIV.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "breadth of validation"}, {"quote": "Additional illustrations, such as ablation or comparison experiments (e.g., investigating the impact of the continuous smoothing function ρ, or examining how the method captures global properties of graphs), would provide a more thorough and solid foundation for the study.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of ablation study"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_KmphHE92wU_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_KmphHE92wU", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper is well-organized and easy to follow.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity and organization"}, {"quote": "The experimental results seem promising.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical performance"}, {"quote": "Authors utilize a novel strategy to softly split the eigenvectors from different eigenspaces, solving the instability constraint of most existing work.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty of stability approach"}, {"quote": "The novelty of the method is somewhat limited, especially the direct application of existing invariant point cloud networks over the eigenvectors without any transfer challenge.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty of method"}, {"quote": "The paper doesn't provide any detail about instance models of ρ, φ, and ψ (in Equations 6 and 7) implemented in the experiments, and doesn't discuss the Lipschitz continuity of these practical models.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of implementation details"}, {"quote": "There is no detail about how OGE-Aug deals with the sign ambiguity of eigenvectors.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of method description"}, {"quote": "Authors don't verify the stability of the OGE-Aug on OOD benchmarks such as DrugOOD [1], where SPE [2] is validated on this dataset.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of stability validation"}, {"quote": "There is no ablation study on the effectiveness of the proposed "soft splitting" strategy.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "missing ablation study"}, {"quote": "There is no experiment studying the sensitivity of hyperparameters.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "lack of sensitivity analysis"}, {"quote": "The paper doesn't report the running time of different positional encoding methods.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "missing efficiency comparison"}, {"quote": "there is no quantitative analysis nor experimental guidance about how to trade off university and stability.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "lack of practical guidance"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_KmphHE92wU_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_KmphHE92wU", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper offers a simple and straightforward way to incorporate Laplacian eigenvectors into GNNs, making it easy to apply to existing architectures.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "ease of application"}, {"quote": "The theoretical result showing that the first approach can achieve universality with a model complexity of n · exp(max(μ)) leverages the sparsity of natural graphs in an interesting way", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "insightfulness of theory"}, {"quote": "The approach is validated with competitive, and in some cases state-of-the-art, results across several common graph benchmarks", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical performance"}, {"quote": "The paper's novelty is somewhat limited. The idea of incorporating Laplacian eigenvectors into MPNNs while respecting the symmetries of the orthogonal group O(d) was already discussed in [2], making the use of point cloud architectures a natural but not particularly novel approach.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty of contribution"}, {"quote": "the way the second model is derived from the first resembles the approach proposed in [1] as well.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "originality of approach"}, {"quote": "The introduction and title of the paper emphasize improved global performance, but this is not explored in depth throughout the rest of the paper.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "alignment of claims and content"}, {"quote": "A more convincing theoretical argument explaining why the proposed model enhances "global expressivity" would be beneficial.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "justification of claims"}, {"quote": "The theory section could be more cohesive.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "coherence of presentation"}, {"quote": "the discussion regarding expressivity primarily focuses on the first model, leaving the expressivity of the second under explored despite being the one used in practice.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of analysis"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_KmphHE92wU_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_KmphHE92wU", "passages": [{"quote": "The proposed OGE-Aug method is theoretically robust, demonstrating strong expressiveness and stability. The underlying motivation is both novel and compelling.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "theoretical soundness and motivation"}, {"quote": "Empirical experiments indicate that OGE-Aug performs competitively and holds promise for real-world applications.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical performance"}, {"quote": "The theoretical contributions of this paper are sufficient, and the proofs appear sound.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "soundness of theory"}, {"quote": "The proposed OGE-Aug method is intricate, highly complex, and challenging to implement.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "implementation complexity"}, {"quote": "the authors present a simplified version using a Cartesian tensor-based point cloud network, which introduces a gap between the theoretical framework and practical implementation.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "theory-practice gap"}, {"quote": "This paper's writing is rough and difficult to read and follow.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of writing"}, {"quote": "symbols such as V are used interchangeably to represent different elements, like sets and matrices, which makes the paper challenging to interpret.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of notation"}, {"quote": "The implementation of OGE-Aug should be presented with more detail, ideally including a pseudocode.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of method description"}, {"quote": "There is no available code to reproduce the results or gain a deeper understanding of the method's details.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "reproducibility"}, {"quote": "some recent state-of-the-art methods, such as Exphormer [1] on the PCQM-Contact dataset, are missing.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of baselines"}, {"quote": "incorporating additional datasets or widely-used benchmarks, such as the OGB benchmark (e.g., ogbg-molhiv, ogbg-molpcba), could further strengthen the evaluation.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "breadth of evaluation"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_oe51Q5Uo37_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_oe51Q5Uo37", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper is well-written and easy to follow.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity of writing"}, {"quote": "a clear explanation of the LoRA-based adapters' role in isolating model layers for efficient data deletion", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity of explanation"}, {"quote": "Validation is performed on a diverse set of tasks and datasets, which strengthens the generalizability performance.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "breadth of validation"}, {"quote": "The technique effectively handles deletion requests under high budgets, with minimal loss in generalizability.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical performance"}, {"quote": "There are some concerns with the proposed top-to-bottom training strategy. First, since different layers are trained with varying data shards, this could cause performance degradation due to inconsistent data exposure across layers.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "soundness of training strategy"}, {"quote": "It would be beneficial to see results when the model is trained from scratch to evaluate this strategy fully.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of evaluation"}, {"quote": "why does a bottom-to-top or other ordering not work well? Some theoretical justification for the chosen order would be helpful.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "justification of design choice"}, {"quote": "It is unclear whether PEFT is essential to this approach or primarily used for computational savings.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of design rationale"}, {"quote": "The novelty of the proposed technique is limited considering the use of off-the-shelf techniques like BMS and LORA to reduce the complexity.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty of contribution"}, {"quote": "A comparison with several recent works like E2URec, Bad-T, NegGrad, NegKL, and RecEraser is missing.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of baselines"}, {"quote": "Why the SISA models do not work in your implementation after 40 requests? (In the original paper, the performance does not even visibly drop for tens of deletion requests).", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "consistency with prior work"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_oe51Q5Uo37_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_oe51Q5Uo37", "passages": [{"quote": "This paper points out a strong limitation of current SISA-based machine unlearning methods: the deletion request of the bottom slices will lead to retraining all the above slices. S3T's solution effectively reduces the re-training time cost.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "significance of contribution"}, {"quote": "The LoRA-based training solution makes S3T practical in application as it is compatible with many Transformer-Based models, including small and large models.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "practicality of approach"}, {"quote": "The theoretical analysis of S3T's deletion rate and performance retention metrics is rigorous.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "rigor of theory"}, {"quote": "The writings and figures of the paper are easy to follow.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity of presentation"}, {"quote": "the paper claims that "approximate unlearning techniques… may have weak privacy guarantees in practice." However, it does not explain whether S3T has a stronger privacy guarantee mechanism.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of privacy analysis"}, {"quote": "it significantly increases the training burden of the model providers (Even after applying the permutation-tree-based method, S3T still requires training the same model multiple times).", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "training cost"}, {"quote": "I think the paper should further explain whether it is worth increasing the training cost several times or even dozens of times to reduce the cost of re-training", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "justification of trade-offs"}, {"quote": "In Section 4.2's evaluation, the uniform deletion prior over all slices may not be enough to fully evaluate the algorithm's performance. The paper could conduct another experiment in which the slice's arrival probability is more unpredictable.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "realism of evaluation"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_oe51Q5Uo37_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_oe51Q5Uo37", "passages": [{"quote": "Theoretically shown that S3T achieves provably better deletion guarantees than existing approaches.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "theoretical contribution"}, {"quote": "Empirical results show that S3T is an effective method for fine-tuning Transformer models, enabling parameter isolation for data slices without compromising the model's performance.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical effectiveness"}, {"quote": "The paper exhibits minor weaknesses due to lack of clarity and ambiguity", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of presentation"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_oe51Q5Uo37_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_oe51Q5Uo37", "passages": [{"quote": "This is a well written paper.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing quality"}, {"quote": "The paper focuses on a very relevant setting involving PEFT for unlearning.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "relevance of problem"}, {"quote": "Rethinking slicing from SISA into a layerwise training while leveraging PEFT is a clever design.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty of design"}, {"quote": "It was interesting to see that such a design does not introduce significant trade-offs.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "balance of approach"}, {"quote": "The experimental evaluation is extensive, spanning several datasets and model sizes.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "breadth of evaluation"}, {"quote": "The authors cover all the important questions relevant to S3T in their evaluations, including its training performance, deletion performance and ablation studies.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "comprehensiveness of evaluation"}, {"quote": "The diversity and scale of experiments strengthens the contributions of the paper.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "strength of empirical validation"}, {"quote": "The appendix discusses several important aspects of the work including storage costs, training time, design choices, etc.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "thoroughness of discussion"}, {"quote": "Depending upon the model and the dataset, S3T can result in lower training performance compared to full training.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "performance trade-off"}, {"quote": "No code is provided, however the authors promise to release it with the final version.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "reproducibility"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_AWg2tkbydO_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_AWg2tkbydO", "passages": [{"quote": "Most other methods based on eigenvectors require computing the eigenbasis, leading to problems on large graphs. In contrast, the authors argue for a worst-case N^2 forward complexity without high preprocessing-complexity.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "computational efficiency"}, {"quote": "The experimental results appear promising.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical performance"}, {"quote": "The paper is not well-integrated into the existing literature. It is unclear what advantages it offers compared to other methods that count cycles.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "positioning in literature"}, {"quote": "the authors do not clearly differentiate their approach or highlight their novel contributions.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of contribution"}, {"quote": "The theoretical results often seem incorrect or lack necessary details.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "soundness of theory"}, {"quote": "many of the results appear to be summaries of theoretical findings from related works.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "originality of theory"}, {"quote": "While the method is more expressive than the 1-WL test, this is not surprising. You can basically do anything to increase beyond 1-WL.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "significance of expressivity result"}, {"quote": "It would be beneficial to include quantitative results, such as whether the method is weaker than the 2-FWL test", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of expressivity analysis"}, {"quote": "although the method is more expressive, it also breaks permutation symmetry.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "theoretical limitation"}, {"quote": "In Section 5, it is unclear what is meant by having a basis as an input.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of explanation"}, {"quote": "Remark 5.1 is incorrect.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "correctness of claim"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_AWg2tkbydO_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_AWg2tkbydO", "passages": [{"quote": "Good motivations: the topic of graph positional encoding is a significant direction, which requires sufficiency, efficiency and easiness for generalization.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem significance"}, {"quote": "The proposed method is easy for plug-in: it proposes positional encodings as aggregation of GNNs' outputs with random/basis inputs, which are quite simple with standard implementation.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "ease of implementation"}, {"quote": "The empirical performance of the proposed method is comparable with SPE methods in Table 2, but it is much more efficient than SPE in Table 1 for larger graphs.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "efficiency advantage"}, {"quote": "Different choices of input with random or basis are good with a consideration of different scales of problems, with the sample size of random inputs examined in Figure 2.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "flexibility of approach"}, {"quote": "A key assumption is missing in proposition 3.1: GSO S is required to be symmetric if we want to use the decomposition in line 105. So the random walk matrix in Eq(2) does not satisfy this condition.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "correctness of theory"}, {"quote": "it might be a little sudden to claim 'SPE can be efficiently implemented by B-PEARL with lower computational and memory complexity': the argument seems coming from the comparison of numbers in Table 2.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "justification of claim"}, {"quote": "it would be better to conduct more careful analysis to provide such a 'subset' or 'equivalence' relationship between the methods", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "rigor of analysis"}, {"quote": "the paper argues ' stability is particularly crucial for out-of-distribution generalization', which is one of the main motivations for this work. However, such a benefit of size generalization is not provided with enough evidence", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "support for motivation"}, {"quote": "in Table 3, the OOD-size performance is not improved by stable methods like SPE and the proposed R-PEARL.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "consistency with claims"}, {"quote": "a 9-layer MPNN is used for experiments, which is relatively deep in the practice of GNNs. Could you please reveal how depth will impact the empirical results?", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "missing ablation study"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_AWg2tkbydO_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_AWg2tkbydO", "passages": [{"quote": "Innovative Approach: The use of message-passing GNNs as nonlinear mappings of eigenvectors is a novel contribution, enabling efficient computation of PEs.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty of approach"}, {"quote": "Comprehensive Analysis: The paper rigorously proves the stability, expressiveness, and computational efficiency of PEARL.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "rigor of analysis"}, {"quote": "Experimental results demonstrate that PEARL outperforms traditional methods on various graph classification and regression tasks while maintaining lower computational complexity.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical performance and efficiency"}, {"quote": "Scalability: The framework is designed to handle large graphs efficiently, addressing a critical limitation of eigenvector-based methods.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "scalability"}, {"quote": "Theoretical Contributions: The analysis of sample complexity and stability provides a solid foundation for the proposed approach.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "theoretical contribution"}, {"quote": "The paper lacks significant research contributions. The authors repeatedly claim high inference speed as a major contribution. While they demonstrate efficient code, they primarily utilize existing codebases.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "limited novelty of contribution"}, {"quote": "the paper could benefit from a deeper discussion on the practical applications of PEARL in real-world scenarios.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "depth of practical discussion"}, {"quote": "The mathematical depth and complexity might pose a barrier to readers unfamiliar with the intricacies of GNNs and spectral graph theory.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "accessibility of presentation"}, {"quote": "additional comparisons with more recent or diverse methods could strengthen the empirical validation.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of baselines"}, {"quote": "further exploration of the impact of different initialization strategies and pooling functions on performance could provide more insights.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "depth of ablation study"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_AWg2tkbydO_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_AWg2tkbydO", "passages": [{"quote": "Good performance on ZINC dataset.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical performance"}, {"quote": "Detailed analysis of R-PEARL.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "depth of analysis"}, {"quote": "The abstract states that this work investigates positional encodings (PEs) for graphs based on four key criteria: stability, expressive power, scalability, and genericness. However, the focus is primarily on eigenvector-based PE, and the analysis is limited to the authors' proposed method, R-PEARL, regarding these criteria. A more comprehensive theoretical analysis and comparison with other PEs are needed.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "breadth of analysis"}, {"quote": "The rationale behind using Message Passing Neural Networks (MPNNs) to generate PEs is not clearly explained.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity of motivation"}, {"quote": "Proposition 3.1 appears to be trivial", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "significance of theoretical result"}, {"quote": "the justification for choosing MPNNs as eigenvalue function over other graph models is not evident.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "justification of design choice"}, {"quote": "While the expectation of R-PEARL is equivariant, the actual R-PEARL method is not, due to the involvement of noise.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "theoretical limitation"}, {"quote": "Theorem 4.3 and the claim that 'our proposed PE framework is well-suited for large-scale graphs' are questionable.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "validity of claim"}, {"quote": "Most theoretical results (Theorem 4.3, Proposition 4.1, 4.2, 4.3) are direct corollories of previous conclusions.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "originality of theory"}, {"quote": "The experimental section is limited to four datasets. To strengthen the validity of the results, additional datasets should be included", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "breadth of evaluation"}, {"quote": "To demonstrate the broad applicability and ensure a fair comparison among different PEs, experiments on PEs with different GNN backbones should be added", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "fairness of comparison"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_AWg2tkbydO_r5", "paper_id": "iclr_AWg2tkbydO", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper addresses an important problem of learning positional encodings on graphs", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem importance"}, {"quote": "The approach of learning PEs as outputs of GNN with random feature inputs on the graph is well-motivated with the observation discussed that GNNs are non-linear functions of eigenvectors of graph shift operators.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "motivation of approach"}, {"quote": "The paper is well-written and presentation is good.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing quality"}, {"quote": "there are no loss functions to bias learning towards such functions. While it is clear the random inputs along with GNN message passing, can encode the relative positional information and the supporting evidence that GNNs compute non-linear maps of eigenvectors of adjacency/laplacians, further regularizing loss functions may be able to make the learning encodings better.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of method design"}, {"quote": "It is not clear to me why eigenvectors need to be used in place of random features for smaller sized graphs. Empirical results to show the difference between eigenvector inputs and random inputs for smaller sized graphs would be beneficial.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "justification of design choice"}, {"quote": "Important works are missing in related work and comparison experiments. In experiments, Random GNN [1] and PF-GNN [2] are not compared, which are highly related", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of baselines"}, {"quote": "The paper claims that the proposed approach is more expressive. Then empirical results showing it is needed. For example, identifying graphs not identifiable by GNNs would be useful.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "validation of expressivity claims"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_qT0IWGqo1j_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_qT0IWGqo1j", "passages": [{"quote": "Proposes a general technique that can be used with any backbone trained with masked language model head. However, the idea is not novel.", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "generality vs novelty"}, {"quote": "The paper has a nice "Related Work" section as well as clear and easy-to-follow narrative.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing quality"}, {"quote": "As acknowledged by the authors, the TTT technique has been used in other domains, however this study applies it for the first time to the computational problems in protein domain.", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "novelty of application"}, {"quote": "One of the motivations of this work is to get rid of additional data collection (MSA) for a given test protein, however the experiments do not show this in a comparable setting.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "validation of motivation"}, {"quote": "there is no comparable setting in which the foundation model is fine-tuned on the sequences homologous to the test protein. Therefore, it is not clear when one should choose to go with TTT instead of MSA", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of comparison"}, {"quote": "It looks like incorporating (co)evolutionary features through fine tuning may be a better option than applying TTT to fog (transformer encoder and masked language model head) for protein fitness prediction.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "strength of results"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_qT0IWGqo1j_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_qT0IWGqo1j", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper is well-motivated. There is an abundance of popular, large, and expensively-trained models by major institutions on massive amounts of protein data that perform "subpar" at best on specific downstream tasks.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "motivation strength"}, {"quote": "Any simple approach that can mitigate this problem, however modestly, can positively influence the future work in this area.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "potential impact"}, {"quote": "The proposed approach avoids being overly complex, and it seems plausible to generalize to downstream tasks not included in the data.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "simplicity and generality"}, {"quote": "The method does not require new labels, an auxillary dataset, or prior knowledge about the tasks.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "practicality of method"}, {"quote": "The main experiments section provides enough data to satisfy the three claimed tasks.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "sufficiency of evidence"}, {"quote": "The experiments prior to the main section (e.g., Figures 3 and 4) substantiate the claims made in the introduction and model description section.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "coherence of validation"}, {"quote": "The paper is quite well-written. I enjoyed reading the paper, understanding the approach and the problem, and the explanations were easy on the mind.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity of writing"}, {"quote": "The key contributions were stated clearly in the introduction, and the abstract and the title are fair representatives of the work.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity of contribution"}, {"quote": "The experimentation quality is reasonable and statistically significant confidence intervals were reported.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "statistical rigor"}, {"quote": "The appendix contains notable valuable and complementary information to the paper; (1) many ablation studies and results for a number of hyper-parameters were included, and (2) the experimental setup is clearly detailed.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "thoroughness of supplementary material"}, {"quote": "The improvements seem modest but consistent across the board, for instance in Table 1.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "consistency of improvements"}, {"quote": "the number of random seeds is a bit on the lower side (i.e., 5 is not too large).", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "statistical robustness"}, {"quote": "My main concern is the proper estimation of the number of test-time training steps.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "guidance on hyperparameters"}, {"quote": "While the paper is not devoid of studies regarding these effects, I don't feel they are complete enough.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of ablation study"}, {"quote": "Some intuitive indications of when and how TTT should be proposed, studied, and tested. There is almost no theoretical component to the paper", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "lack of theoretical guidance"}, {"quote": "A more thorrough discussion and experimental results regarding the **limitations** of the approach is also missing from the paper.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "discussion of limitations"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_qT0IWGqo1j_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_qT0IWGqo1j", "passages": [{"quote": "Good attempt at biological problems.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "domain applicability"}, {"quote": "The rationale for selecting the current TTT methods is unclear. Provide a clear justification for the choice.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "justification of method choice"}, {"quote": "The objectives should be linked to improved biological performance. Add relevant goals to achieve desired outcomes.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "biological relevance of objectives"}, {"quote": "Reducing perplexity is insufficient for justifying large model use.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "justification of model size"}, {"quote": "Finetuning large models is resource-intensive. Assess cost-effectiveness and seek more efficient training strategies.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "resource efficiency"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_qT0IWGqo1j_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_qT0IWGqo1j", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper is clearly written and organized.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity and organization"}, {"quote": "The method is described clearly and is well-motivated by existing literature.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity of method description"}, {"quote": "The figures are nicely designed and clearly convey the intended information.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "quality of figures"}, {"quote": "The evaluations covers a broad range of tasks in fitness prediction.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "breadth of evaluation"}, {"quote": "The method is motivated by models with "Y-shaped" architectures in which there is both an MLM head and a fitness prediction head. However, the authors evaluate on the zero-shot task in ProteinGym, where models use masked token probabilities as proxies for fitness predictions and therefore do not use a Y-shaped architecture. This is confusing", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "alignment of motivation and evaluation"}, {"quote": "The paper would be improved by evaluating on the fine-tuning tasks in ProteinGym or by more clearly explaining why the zero-shot task is more appropriate.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "justification of evaluation choice"}, {"quote": "These arguments are situational and are not strong enough reasons to avoid direct comparisons with the cited methods.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "justification for excluding baselines"}, {"quote": "The paper would be strengthened by including a more in-depth discussion about the distinction between existing methods and the authors' proposed method", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "depth of comparison"}, {"quote": "it does suggest that the MSA-based adaption of TranceptEVE can have advantages over TTT, which warrants further investigation", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "completeness of comparison"}, {"quote": "The result on improving structure prediction in ESM3 and ESMFold is interesting, but of limited practical relevance since AlphaFold2/3 are far superior structure predictors.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "practical relevance of results"}, {"quote": "the authors claim in section 3.3 to offer an explanation for the effectiveness of test time adaptation by appealing to the correlation between perplexity minimization and model performance. This is somewhat circular", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "logical soundness of explanation"}]}
{"review_id": "ANCH-2", "paper_id": "ANCH-2", "passages": [{"quote": "This submission provides a rigorous theoretical analysis; the proofs appear correct and the assumptions are clearly stated.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "rigor of theory"}, {"quote": "The related-work coverage is adequate.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "coverage of related work"}, {"quote": "My main concern is reproducibility: no code is provided and several hyperparameters are unreported.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "reproducibility"}, {"quote": "Overall the significance for the broader community seems modest.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "significance of contribution"}]}
